{"path":"numeric/math/isunordered","title":"isunordered","titleHtml":"isunordered","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/isunordered","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Determines if the floating point numbers x and y are unordered, that is, one or both are NaN and thus cannot be meaningfully compared with each other.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math\"><code>&lt;math.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c99\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"co2\">#define isunordered(x, y) /* implementation defined */</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(since C99)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Determines if the floating point numbers <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">x</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">y</span></code> are unordered, that is, one or both are NaN and thus cannot be meaningfully compared with each other.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> floating point value\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> y\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> floating point value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Nonzero integral value if either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">x</span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">y</span></code> is NaN, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> otherwise.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"isunordered(NAN,1.0) =&nbsp;%d<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, isunordered<span class=\"br0\">(</span>NAN, <span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"isunordered(1.0,NAN) =&nbsp;%d<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, isunordered<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span>, NAN<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"isunordered(NAN,NAN) =&nbsp;%d<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, isunordered<span class=\"br0\">(</span>NAN, NAN<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"isunordered(1.0,0.0) =&nbsp;%d<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, isunordered<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>isunordered(NAN,1.0) = 1\nisunordered(1.0,NAN) = 1\nisunordered(NAN,NAN) = 1\nisunordered(1.0,0.0) = 0</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-23\">\n<ul><li> C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.14.6 The isunordered macro (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.10.11 Comparison macros (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.14.6 The isunordered macro (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.10.11 Comparison macros (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.14.6 The isunordered macro (p: 261)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> F.10.11 Comparison macros (p: 531)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.12.14.6 The isunordered macro (p: 242)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/fpclassify\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>fpclassify</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   classifies the given floating-point value  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function macro)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/isnan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>isnan</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c99\">(C99)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if the given number is NaN <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function macro)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/isunordered\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>isunordered</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics"},{"path":"numeric/math","title":"Common mathematical functions"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"isunordered","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Determines if the floating point numbers x and y are unordered, that is, one or both are NaN and thus cannot be…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"x, y"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Nonzero integral value if either x or y is NaN, 0 otherwise."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"fpclassify","note":"classifies the given floating-point value"},{"label":"isnan","note":"checks if the given number is NaN"}]}]},"standards":["C99"],"wordCount":190,"codeBlockCount":2}
